        "stem": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "When the water supply to a plant is reduced, the concentration of abscisic acid (ABA) in the leaves increases.",
            "source": {
              "qp": 22
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "ABA binds to receptors in the cell surface membranes of guard cells. This triggers a series of events in the cells, which results in stomatal closure.",
            "source": {
              "qp": 22
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Fig. 8.1 is a diagram of part of a guard cell showing some of the events that occur when ABA binds to its receptor.",
            "source": {
              "qp": 22
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "figure",
            "id": "fig8.1",
            "caption": "Fig. 8.1",
            "src": "figures/q8_fig8_1.png",
            "alt": "ABA signalling in a guard cell",
            "source": {
              "qp": 22
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Fig. 8.1 shows that calcium ions are involved in the events within a guard cell that result in stomatal closure.",
            "source": {
              "qp": 22
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Outline the role of calcium ions in the response of the guard cell to a reduced water supply <b>and</b> explain how this response results in stomatal closure.",
            "source": {
              "qp": 22
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Identify <b>X</b> in your answer.",
            "source": {
              "qp": 22
            }
          }
        ],
        "marks": 4,
        "topics": [
